# The scraped corpus never goes into git. It holds real text from real retailer pages —
# scrubbed, but not audited line by line — and roughly 30 MB of third-party marketing copy
# is a volume problem even when it is a privacy-clean one. The leading slash matters: the
# bare pattern also matched research/corpus/, which is hand-written and meant to be tracked.
/corpus/

# Ad-hoc probe scripts. They drive live retailer sites and are written to be thrown away;
# publishing scraping one-offs under a project about retailer ethics is an own-goal.
__*.mjs

